  "requirement": "B14 (RS B14; PLAN-S:172; stage-1 pre-registration DRAFT revision 2 section 9.4, with the 'holds' rule of S-25 and CONS LS-19): the sealed split of the evaluation prompts into a lower-similarity and a higher-similarity half per add set, and the report of the add effect on each half",
  "rule": {
    "boundary_ties": "higher",
    "rule": "per add set, over the n evaluation prompts: k = floor(n / 2); b = the (k + 1)-th smallest S(e; A); the lower-similarity half = the prompts with S < b; the higher-similarity half = the prompts with S >= b. Equal values (exact float equality) at the boundary all go to the higher half, so every lower-half prompt is strictly less similar than every higher-half prompt; the lower half then holds fewer than k prompts, and the record says how many tied",
    "sealed": "strata.json is written once, by SHA-256, before any add-arm outcome is read; the report reads it only by that SHA-256"
  },
